v(9) > 9,121,002: certificates for every integer 3000001 <= m <= 10000000 except 8 primes (2026-09-22)

stage                                                               integers settled
three-way split of a 7-term representation, code/threesplit.c           6,999,957
direct search, code/findm.c (K = 9, work cap 2e7)                              15
one-term split of an 8-term representation, code/split_stage.py                 3
p-adic families, code/padic_jobs.py + code/findfrac.c, j, l <= 300              10
p-adic families, j, l <= 3000                                                    7
                                                                     total   6,999,992

The 25 integers left after the first three stages were all primes p with p - 1 missing at k = 8.
For such p, the other multiples of p in a 9-term representation must cancel the 1/p p-adically.
The two simplest ways:
  one multiple:  p(jp - 1), and the other 7 terms sum to 1 - j/(jp - 1)
  two multiples: p k1, p k2 with (k1 + 1)(k2 + 1) = 1 + l p, and the other 6 terms sum to 1 - l/(k1 k2)
padic_jobs.py lists these subproblems and findfrac.c searches each one.
Replacing two terms of a 7-term representation by three (1/a + 1/b = 1/m + 1/x + 1/y, all 245,765
representations, every pair) was also tried on the 25 and settled none.

No certificate yet (j, l <= 3000 exhausted with a work cap of 2e6 per subproblem):
